---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import EditorialPage from '../components/EditorialPage.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Use — Kidtivity Lab"
  description="Terms governing your use of Kidtivity Lab and its activity resources."
>
  <EditorialPage
    eyebrow="Using Kidtivity Lab"
    title="Terms of Use"
    lede="These terms set the ground rules for using our website, activity instructions, printables, and related resources."
    currentLabel="Terms of Use"
    updated="July 26, 2026"
  >
    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>1. Acceptance of these terms</h2>
      <p>
        By accessing or using Kidtivity Lab, you agree to these Terms of Use and our
        <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree, please do not use the website.
      </p>
      <p>
        The website is intended for adults, including parents, caregivers, and educators. Children
        should use any website content only with an adult’s involvement and supervision.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>2. Informational purpose</h2>
      <p>
        Kidtivity Lab provides general activity ideas and educational information. It is not a
        substitute for medical, developmental, occupational therapy, educational, legal, or other
        professional advice. We do not diagnose conditions or guarantee developmental outcomes.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>3. Adult judgment and child safety</h2>
      <p>
        You are responsible for deciding whether an activity is appropriate for a particular child,
        space, material, and situation. Age ranges are general guidance, not safety guarantees.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide active adult supervision appropriate to the child and activity.</li>
        <li>Check materials for choking, allergy, toxicity, sharp-edge, burn, water, and fall hazards.</li>
        <li>Follow manufacturer instructions for products and equipment.</li>
        <li>Stop immediately if a child is distressed, unwell, or using materials unsafely.</li>
        <li>Adapt or skip any activity that does not suit the child’s abilities or environment.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="note-box">
        Safety notes on activity pages highlight common concerns, but they cannot identify every
        possible risk or replace attentive adult supervision.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>4. Permitted use</h2>
      <p>
        You may view, print, and use Kidtivity Lab materials for personal, family, or individual
        classroom use, unless a resource states otherwise.
      </p>
      <p>You may not, without written permission:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>republish, sell, sublicense, or commercially distribute our content or printables;</li>
        <li>copy substantial portions of the website into another database, app, or publication;</li>
        <li>remove copyright, attribution, disclosure, or safety notices;</li>
        <li>scrape or access the site in a way that disrupts service or bypasses technical controls;</li>
        <li>misrepresent Kidtivity Lab content as your own or imply our endorsement.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>5. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The website design, original text, illustrations, activity presentation, downloadable
        resources, branding, and compilations are owned by or licensed to Kidtivity Lab and are
        protected by applicable intellectual-property laws. Third-party names and trademarks
        remain the property of their respective owners.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>6. Affiliate links and advertising</h2>
      <p>
        Some pages may contain affiliate links. If you purchase through one of those links, we may
        receive a commission at no additional cost to you. Affiliate relationships do not change
        the price you pay and do not guarantee that a product is suitable for your child.
      </p>
      <p>
        We aim to place clear disclosures near relevant recommendations. Sponsored content, if
        introduced, will be identified as such.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>7. Third-party services and links</h2>
      <p>
        The website may link to retailers, email providers, printable-delivery services, or other
        third parties. We do not control their availability, security, content, products, or
        privacy practices. Your use of third-party services is governed by their terms.
      </p>
